I finally found the cause and the solution of my problem:

after disassembling and reassembling the drive again, I discovered a gap in
the black plastic guard at the back of the drive, which should cover the
tape. This gap contains some sensors (possibly to detect the wholes in the
tape leader), but the tape was running outside this gap. I think, I had some
problems with the TK50 tape, where the tape lead wasn't caught by the hook
and got wind up on the reel. I must have missed this gap when reinserting
the tape lead.
After fixing this problem, the tape drive is working as usual.

regards,
Winfried




