> - PDP11/23+, KDF11-BA (M8189)
> has -BA ROM but need to up it to -BJ for TK50 boot  

A standard 11/23+ has pretty basic boot ROMs in it, not unlike a BDV11.
The microPDP-11/23 had various ROMs:

23-339E2/23-340E2  = -BA    PDP11/23+
23-158E4/23-159E4  = -BE(?) earliest microPDP-11/23
23-238E4/23-239E4  = -BE    microPDP-11/23
23-183E4/23-184E4  = -BF    microPDP-11/23
23-380E4/23-381E4  = -BG   (called -BH in the Maintenance Manual)
23-453E4/23-454E4  = -BJ   (last release)

I have images of 23-339E2 and 23-340E2, 23-183E4 and 23-184E4, and
23-453E4 and 23-454E4.

I'd like to get images of 23-158E4 and 23-159E4, 23-238E4 and 23-239E4,
and 23-380E4 and 23-381E4.  I'm also looking for some of the VT100
ROMs, KDJ-11 ROMs (23-116E5/23-117E5), and early RQDX2 ROMs
(23-178E5/23-179E5)

> - LSI-II/73, KDJ11-AA (M8192)
> ROMless, so I am sourcing for the MXV11-B2 bootstrap ROM option

Those are 23-145E4 and 23-146E4, which I have.

Although the only real difference (apart from packaging) between a
PDP-11/23+ and a microPDP-11/23 is the ROMs, you'll have to change some
jumpers.  The E2 on the older ROMs signifies 2K x 8 size, while the E4
means 8K x 8.



