On 2004-02-29, Hans Vlems <hvlems.dotweg@zonnet.nl> wrote:
> Yesterday I managed to rescue a Mylex DAC960 controler from a Digital server
> 5200. That's an Intel based system, and I wondered whether it useful on an
> Alpha (3000 or 5305) with VMS.

The options list for the Alphaserver 1000A lists it as supported. I don't
know if it would be in a later machine, but don't see why not.

> The controller is labeled DAC960PDU and has 4 MB memory on board. It has one
> internal 68 pin SCSI connector and one connector (rather smallish, 1 1/4"
> long, 1/8" wide) on the bulkead. Both labeled CHN0 (channel 0 ?).

It's a simgle-channel controller, and probably has support for only 7
drives.

> The questions are:
> 1) is there a manual available for this device?

Dunno. I never found one. Google for SWXCR or KZPSC.

> 2) will it work with Alpha/VMS (7.3) ?

I suspect it will, but there's only one way to find out.

You'll need to download
ftp://ftp.compaq.com/pub/softpaq/alphant/m-arcapp.zip , which has two
utilities. ARCCF.EXE is the configuration utility, and ARCFL.EXE is the
firmware update. Noth are run from the ARC console or AlphaBIOS "Run a
program" menu selection. On the 1000A, you reach the ARC console by issuing
the "arc" command at the SRM prompt; I don't know about the 3000/5305, nor
abot whether you can switch (in either direction) without reflashing.


