The SOC mentioned earlier in this thread has memory information (as do all
SOC's that I've seen:

Step 4-Memory 
Selection of a minimum of 128 MB memory is mandatory for CTO systems 
Systems support 128 MB to 2 GB system memory (two memory banks support four
DIMMs per bank).

SN-MSP01-KA
128 MB ECC memory DIMMs (4 x 32MB DIMMs)
SN-MSP01-KB
256 MB ECC memory DIMMs (4 x 64MB DIMMs)
SN-MSP01-KC
512 MB ECC memory DIMMs (4 x 128MB DIMMs)
SN-MSP01-KD
1024 MB ECC memory DIMMs (4 x 256MB DIMMs)

As implied elsewhere in this thread, visiting 3rd-party memory suppliers such
as crucial.com, and inputting the above-named part numbers, can sometimes yield
equivalent (and cheaper) memory parts.  I've used crucial parts in my PWS 433au
for several years without incident; I've seen other threads where folks have
supplied similar testimonials for other 3rd-party vendors.  Of course, if your
machine or app is mission-critical, then it's best to go with
Digital/COMPAQ/hp-recommended parts.	:-)

