I'm surprised that this isn't in the VMS FAQ, but I looked through it
and didn't find it anywhere.

In fact, the problem started with wanting to read the FAQ, in
bookreader format.  I found a link for downloading the FAQ in
bookreader format at

http://h71000.www7.hp.com/wizard/faq/vmsfaq.decw$book

and downloaded it using Mozilla 1.4 on OpenVMS Alpha 7.3-1 with TCPIP
version 5.3 on a PWS600AU.  Then I tried to open the file using the
bookreader program that came with DECWindows (Motif) and I get the
error message "Error reading field in record" and it won't open.

I guessed from the error message that the problem was that Mozilla
downloaded the file in the wrong format.  With ANALYZE/RMS_FILE/FDL I
was able to determine that Mozilla had created a sequential file with
fixed-length records of 512 bytes each.  Then I found some bookreader
files that came with the operating system and discovered that they are
sequential files containing variable length records.

So I editing the FDL that ANALYZE/RMS_FILE/FDL had created for my
downloaded file so that the RECORD section that had read 

RECORD
	BLOCK_SPAN		yes
	CARRIAGE_CONTROL	none
	FORMAT			fixed
	SIZE			512

would read

RECORD
	BLOCK_SPAN		yes
	CARRIAGE_CONTROL	none
	FORMAT			variable
	SIZE			0

and ran CONVERT/FDL.  Guess what?  CONVERT created a file containing
variable-length records that all just happen to contain exactly 512
bytes (i.e. one-for-one the original block structure) and bookreader
gives me the same error.

I think that fundamentally the problem here is that when I downloaded
the file, I didn't get the meta-data that describe the record
structure.  Since they are variable-length records, there really is no
way of guessing what the lengths are unless there is some other sort
of record delimiter in there.

Does anybody have a solution for this?

Chip

-- 
Charles  M. "Chip" Coldwell
