Shipping things overseas is easy, you don't have to worry about imaginary
blacklists.  Any Fedex, UPS, or USPS service counter can help you ship
things which aren't too big.  The UPS/Fedex weight limit on express packages
is 150lbs. I believe.  The only differences between sending items within the
US/Canada and anywhere else in the world are 1.  Service rates are higher
(most likely no one in their right mind would pay to have something that
heavy shipped that far), and 2.  you have to fill out a customs declaration
(UPS/Fedex/USPS have the forms available) indicating your name and address,
the recipient's name and address, package contents, final country 
destination, and declared value.  I've never had any problems with customs
holding up merchandise, and I've sent computers/related garbage all over 
Europe/Asia/South America/etc...  Mostly the extra form is there to ensure
the recipient gets screwed over with various custom's duties (make sure the
paperwork indicates the recipient should be billed for any duties imposed by
the country of destination).  

