Seriously though, I think Mr Henderson might be able to reduce the 46 inch
depth. But I doubt that the height and width could be reduced. (and one should
also add the wheels to this).

I know how I can reduce the cabinet of my all mighty microvax II because I
have disassembled it (and disassembled the cabinet of a spare MVII to house my
stereo equipment.

Unless you are a certified DEC technician, you are unlikely to have thinkered
with a 2100 at the office to a point where you are intimate with he cabinet.
That leaves bobbyists who would have a 2100 and would have looked under the
cabinet's clothes to see what's under the hood and could therefore comment on
if the cab can be made smaller.

Sorry, but I think that Mr Henderson has a valid question. He could have asked
about making the cab smaller to fit some industrial application and the
answers should have been the same.


